4:49)"},"v2_02_complete_repository_suite_consumed":true,"v2_02_controlling_plan_revision":"R1","v2_02_decision_1_amendment_authority":"ACCEPT AND AUTHORIZE THE DECISION 1 AMENDMENT — BOUNDED V2 DEVELOPMENT VALIDATOR COMPATIBILITY CORRECTION AND E0/W1 RECOVERY — EXACTLY AS PRESENTED IN THE CURRENT REVIEW PACKET.\n\nTHE AUTHORITATIVE STARTING CHECKPOINT REMAINS:\n\nCOMMIT:\ne69699fa4cc77e3a34cc35e522c23cb2f1260ccf\n\nTREE:\n5e6818ede0d3f387425edf78cd54d7bdce7ac2ae\n\nBRANCH:\nfeature/v2-continuity-onboarding\n\nWORKTREE:\nD:\\A\\Floppy-V2\n\nAUTHORIZE THE EXACT RECOVERY SEQUENCE:\n\n1. VERIFY THE EXACT PRESERVED STOPPED LOCAL STATE.\n2. COMPLETE THE ALREADY-AUTHORIZED E0 ONE-PATH MANIFEST EVIDENCE CORRECTION.\n3. COMMIT, VALIDATE, NORMALLY PUSH, AND VERIFY E0.\n4. APPLY EXACTLY ONE BOUNDED_VALIDATOR_CORRECTION REUSABLE-PRODUCT COMMIT LIMITED TO tools/validate_floppy.py, system-manifest.json, and tests/test_tooling.py.\n5. VALIDATE THAT CORRECTION THROUGH THE EXISTING NO-ACTIVE-AUTHORITY BOUNDED_VALIDATOR_CORRECTION INTEGRITY ROUTE.\n6. NORMALLY PUSH THE VALIDATED CORRECTION AND VERIFY LOCAL/REMOTE EQUALITY AND A CLEAN WORKTREE.\n7. ONLY THEN APPLY W1 / TR-002-ACCEPT-WORK-PACKAGE FOR V2-02 USING THE EXACT FIVE-PATH CONTROL SCOPE DEFINED IN THE PACKET.\n8. VALIDATE AND NORMALLY PUSH W1.\n9. STOP WITH V2-02 ACCEPTED AS THE PLANNING BASELINE, IMPLEMENTATION NOT STARTED, NO ACTIVE IMPLEMENTATION AUTHORIZATION, AND NO REPOSITORY WRITER.\n\nTHE VALIDATOR CORRECTION MUST BE GENERIC FOR THE ORDERED V2 ROADMAP. IT MUST NOT BE A SPECIAL-CASE V2-02 BYPASS. PREVIOUS PACKAGES MUST BE CLOSED; THE CURRENT PACKAGE MUST HOLD A LAWFUL CURRENT OPERATIONAL STATUS; LATER PACKAGES MUST REMAIN PLANNED_NOT_AUTHORIZED; SKIPPED-PACKAGE PROGRESSION AND PREMATURE LATER-PACKAGE ADVANCEMENT ARE FORBIDDEN; CLOSED EARLIER PACKAGES MUST NOT BE REWRITTEN.\n\nTHE THREE-PATH CORRECTION MUST NOT APPLY THE CLASS-B SUPERSESSION, IMPLEMENT V2-02 P1, MODIFY V1 SCHEMAS, MODIFY project-seed/.floppy/*, CREATE AN AUTHORIZATION, CREATE A REPOSITORY WRITER, OR CHANGE LIFECYCLE STATE.\n\nDO NOT EXECUTE OR CONSUME THE V2-02 COMPLETE REPOSITORY TEST-SUITE AUTHORIZATION DURING THIS RECOVERY.\n\nDO NOT MODIFY main. DO NOT APPLY CLASS-B S1. DO NOT IMPLEMENT V2-02 P1. DO NOT CREATE V2_02_IMPLEMENTATION. DO NOT CREATE V2_02_WORKING_MODEL. DO NOT MIGRATE, INTEGRATE, MERGE, TAG, RELEASE, REBASE, FORCE-PUSH, RESET DESTRUCTIVELY, OR REWRITE HISTORY.","v2_02_decision_1_utf8_followup_authority":"AUTHORIZE DECISION 1 FOLLOW-UP — SECOND BOUNDED VALIDATOR CORRECTION FOR UTF-8 GIT-INTEGRITY DECODING, SUBJECT TO THE ADDITIONAL VC1 RE-PROOF REQUIREMENT BELOW.\n\nPRESERVE THE EXISTING LOCAL VC1 COMMIT EXACTLY AS CREATED.\n\nDO NOT AMEND, REBASE, RESET, REWRITE, SQUASH, DISCARD, OR RECREATE VC1.\n\nAUTHORIZE ONE ADDITIONAL STATE-PRESERVING `BOUNDED_VALIDATOR_CORRECTION` COMMIT, VC2, LIMITED EXACTLY TO:\n\n- `tools/validate_floppy.py`\n- `system-manifest.json`\n- `tests/test_tooling.py`\n\nVC2 MAY ONLY:\n\n1. make `_git_integrity_run()` explicitly decode Git stdout/stderr as UTF-8 with deterministic error handling;\n2. add regression coverage proving Unicode `.floppy/manifest.json` content retrieved from committed Git revisions remains semantically equal to the UTF-8 working-tree manifest;\n3. update only the required validator SHA-256 registrations in `system-manifest.json`.\n\nTHE REGRESSION TEST MUST EXERCISE THE ACTUAL GIT-INTEGRITY MANIFEST-COMPARISON PATH THAT PRODUCED `GIT_INTEGRITY_CANDIDATE_MANIFEST_MISMATCH` AND `GIT_INTEGRITY_BOUNDED_CORRECTION_MANIFEST_CHANGED`; A TEST OF `_git_integrity_run()` ALONE IS NOT SUFFICIENT.\n\nBEFORE VC2, VERIFY REMOTE FEATURE BRANCH EQUALS E0 06a9cf185601e5870089f62f7c2e695ec720bd68; LOCAL HEAD IS EXACTLY ONE COMMIT ABOVE E0 WITH E0 AS PARENT; SUBJECT IS `fix(v2): generalize V2 development progression validation`; VC1 CHANGES EXACTLY tools/validate_floppy.py, system-manifest.json, tests/test_tooling.py; WORKTREE CLEAN; VC1 SOURCE VALIDATION AND GENERIC V2 P